# The alpha tree PAX carries as /bin/alpha (tools/mkalpha builds it).
#
# alpha is the service manager for PAX, in wolf (wolffe-lang/alpha): units
# in a strict format of its own (its docs/UNIT-1.md), checked by `alpha
# check`, started and supervised by `alpha manager`, asked over a control
# socket (its docs/CONTROL-1.md). PAX stages it with nothing to start: no
# unit ships and nothing runs it at boot, so /bin/alpha is a program a
# person types. PAX reads no more of its tree than building it needs.
#
# alpha 2aaf3f8 (2026-11-21): `tools/build --static`, the static ET_EXEC
# PAX runs, checked by alpha's own gate. Pinned in its own
# wolf-toolchain.toml at wolf 0.2.40 / lupin 0.1.62 / wolf-std c339a471,
# a std newer than the one the wolf archive bundles (alpha's event loop is
# built on its std.poll). tools/mkalpha builds it with THAT toolchain,
# the std fetched at its commit and its tree checked, through alpha's own
# tools/build --static, in two checkouts, refusing two digests, and ships
# the stripped copy.
ALPHA_REPO=https://github.com/wolffe-lang/alpha
ALPHA_REV=2aaf3f8b572e4898638440f2558e1a69fa4271d4
